    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n1. **`src/finetune/index.js`** - Added named exports for the schema constants that the test imports:\n   - `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n   - `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n   - `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n   - `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n   The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly from the module, but it was only available via the default export. Adding named exports allows the test to use destructuring imports.\n\n2. **`src/eval/metrics.js`** - Fixed the `toxicityMetric` function to correctly handle the `references` parameter:\n   - Changed the function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n   - The function now always uses `defaultBannedTerms` instead of treating the second parameter as custom banned terms\n   \n   This was necessary because `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but the toxicity metric doesn't need references\u2014it should always use the default list of banned keywords.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across 8 test files. The existing public exports remain unchanged and working.",
